// Checkpoint saves without stopping the game: `save_world_bg` takes
// a copy of the world where it stands (a memory copy, milliseconds)
// and a thread of its own (saver.c) writes that copy to `Saved.file`;
// `save_world_poll`, a tick later or a few, puts how it went in
// `Saved.ok`; `save_world_join` waits for a write still going (before
// a `load_world` reads one of the files). Where a write is still
// going when the next checkpoint comes, that checkpoint is skipped:
// its slot keeps the world of the one before, which a replay can
// still start from.
import world

extern system save_world_bg()
extern system save_world_poll()
extern system save_world_join()
